  "note": "Chara Dasha sets the period; a slow transit occupying or aspecting the dasha Rasi / AL narrows it; transits never override an inactive Rasi. Aspects are Jaimini Rasi Drishti (sign to sign, mutual), not Parashari graha drishti. Argala here is a transit in the 2nd/4th/11th (primary) or 5th (secondary) from the reference; obstructed_by lists the natal planets in the Virodha sign (12th/10th/3rd/9th) \u2014 whether they outweigh the Argala is an interpretive call. double_transit is sampled at window start/mid/end only; use the Jupiter and Saturn sign_stays for exact overlap dates. reference.antardasha_rasi is the Antardasha running at window start; each annotation reads house_from_antardasha_rasi from the Antardasha running at that snapshot / stay entry (antardasha_rasi_used).",
  "karakamsha_overlay_note": "Placing a transit in D9 by its nakshatra pada (one pada = one navamsha) and comparing with Karakamsha is a lineage-specific practice, not Jaimini Sutra text; offered as a secondary signal only."
